### Determinization

For finite state automaton $A = (\Sigma, Q, I, \delta, F)$, we can construct an equivalent, deterministic finite state automaton $A' = (\Sigma, Q', I', \delta', F')$ over the same symbols $\Sigma$ by the _subset construction_ algorithm, called so as the states `Q'` become sets of states of `Q`. The algorithm iteratively visits all states of `Q` and adds states to `Q'` by merging states of `Q`, and adds transitions to $\delta'$ by transforming those of $\delta$:

```
procedure determinize(A: FiniteStateAutomaton) → FiniteStateAutomaton
    I' := {A.I}
    Q', δ', V := {I'}, {}, {}
    while Q' ≠ V do
        q' :∈ Q' – V ; V := V ∪ {q'}
        for a ∈ A.Σ do
            r' := A.δ̂ q' a
            if r' ≠ {} then Q' := Q' ∪ {r'}; δ' q' a := r'
    F' := {q' ∈ Q' | q' ∩ A.F ≠ ∅}
    return (A.Σ, Q', I', δ', F')
```

